"summary_desc":"There are two groups of workings: 1. An overgrown, collapsed adit (or adits) striking about 050 deg T. 2. three unfilled ?shafts in a 30 m long line trending 040 deg T. Reef trending at 140 deg T, (right angles to the adit) (Gilligan and Brownlow 1987).","size_code":"OCC","major_comm":"Au","minor_comm":null,"ore_min":null,"gangue_min":"quartz","hostrocks":null,"reference":"Gilligan L.B. & Brownlow J.W. (1987) ;  Gilligan L.B., Brownlow J.W. & Cameron R.G. (1987) ;  Titles, Mineral Resources NSW () ","compiler":"IBL Paterson, January 1978","production":null,"resources":null,"gs_number":null,"colour":"red","is_metmin_resource":"n"},"bbox":[151.1623,-31.4642,151.1623,-31.4642]},{"type":"Feature","id":"mineral_occurrence.151646","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[151.1633,-31.4678]},"geometry_name":"geom","properties":{"occurrence_id":151646,"deposit_name":"Wrights Spur Reef","comm_type":"METMIN","field_no":"ND0027","metal_no":"TH0183","old_no":"TH0183","metal_dist":"Nundle","all_names":"Wrights Spur Reef","latgda94":-31.467825,"longda94":151.163291,"ll_coordsys":"GDA94","loc_method":"250K","accuracy":250,"grid_loc":null,"mga_north":6517089,"mga_east":325505,"mga_coordsys":"MGA_56S","length":120,"width":null,"depth":11,"dep_dip_plunge":null,"dep_dip_dir":70,"strike":160,"work_desc":"Underground workings, open cut, shafts and adits,","dep_shape":null,"structure":"shear","host_relate":null,"msn_style":"vein","ore_texture":null,"alteration":null,"placer":null,"spec_model":"vein","gen_model":"hydrothermal","cox_class":null,"other_class":"metahydrothermal - Au (quartz vein)","nsw_class":"Structurally controlled low sulfide Au","nsw_gen":"Hydrothermal metamorphic Au","summary_desc":"The dumps are moderately extensive; the workings have all collapsed. The quartz is vughy in places, and cherty in others. Edwards and Wilson put in a 60 m drive for very little return. What Wright and Taylor did is not known (Gilligan and Brownlow 1987).","size_code":"SML","